                            InterWorld 
                               v1.0
                               

This is an executable demo of the InterWorld.  It is an interactive Virtual
Reality enviornment to exapand on.  This demo is just to see some of the
features in action.  The renderer is REND386 with added functions to 
handle all the Room and collision stuff.  The .C Source code can be found
in the CyberForum VR Code Workgroup lib.  I am hoping anyone out there
with an interest in VR and has Borland C++ 3.1 will grab the source and
expand the world!  That is the whole purpose.  In your room you can
add anything you want, disk maint. routines - data visualization - whatever 
you can dream up.

The functions I have created are very easy to use and everything is already
in a shell.  You can simply add your stuff to the functions you want to
use and they will be executed.  There is already one wing (East Wing) defined
as an example that you can use to go on.  Just cut and paste to add your
own stuff.

All the source code is documented to show you where and what to do with
the functions.  To see more about the code'ing see code.doc that is in 
the source code archive.

To move around the world just use your arrow keys or joystick.  There is
no collision detection on the walls so you must be sure to run into the
'icons' to get from one place to another.  It is easy to use and keep
orientation.  You can also click on objects to get their names.

